OL,3,AChemistry Nobel awarded for solving
OL,4,Amystery of life's asymmetry
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Nobel Prize in Chemistry has been
OL,7,Fawarded to French scientist Henri B.
OL,8,FKagan and Japan's Kenso Soai for
OL,9,Fproviding a solution to the chemical
OL,10,Fmystery of life's asymmetry.
OL,12,FThe Nobel Committee explained:
OL,13,F"Molecules used by all life, such as
OL,14,Fthe amino acids that are building of
OL,15,Fproteins, are what is known as chiral.
OL,17,F"This means that they have two versions
OL,18,Fthat are mirror images of one another."
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
